"CSS Pseudo-Elements Module Level 4 (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo-4/)\nciteturn3600view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo-4/\",\"pattern\":\"fully styleable pseudo-elements\"}); Total lines: 1512\nL356: #### 2.2.4. Styling the First-Letter Pseudo-elements\nL357: \nL358: In CSS a 【25†::first-letter】 【81†pseudo-element】 (and its 【23†::prefix】 and 【24†::suffix】 sub-elements) is similar to an 【334†inline box】. The following properties apply to ::first-letter, ::first-letter::prefix, and ::first-letter::suffix pseudo-elements:\nL740: ## 4. Tree-Abiding Pseudo-elements\nL741: \nL742: Tree-abiding pseudo-elements always fit within the box tree. They 【196†inherit】 any inheritable properties from their 【83†originating element】; non-inheritable properties take their 【745†initial values】 as usual. 【816†[CSS-CASCADE-4]】 A subset of these are the fully styleable pseudo-elements; all properties that apply to a real element also apply to a 【817†fully styleable pseudo-element】.\nL743: \nL744: Tests\nL745:   * 【818†tree-abiding-pseudo-elements.html†wpt.fyi】 【819†(live test)†wpt.live】 【820†(source)†github.com】\nL746: ### 4.1. Generated Content Pseudo-elements: 【330†::before】 and 【331†::after】\nL747: \nL748: When their computed 【821†content】 value is not 【822†none】, these 【81†pseudo-elements】 generate boxes as if they were immediate children of their 【83†originating element】, with content as specified by content.\nL749: ::before\nL750:     Represents a styleable child pseudo-element immediately before the 【83†originating element】’s actual content.\nL751: ::after\nL752:     Represents a styleable child pseudo-element immediately after the 【83†originating element】’s actual content.\nL753: Tests\nL754:   * 【823†before-after-dynamic-custom-property-001.html†wpt.fyi】 【824†(live test)†wpt.live】 【825†(source)†github.com】\nL755:   * 【826†before-as-flex-container.html†wpt.fyi】 【827†(live test)†wpt.live】 【828†(source)†github.com】\nL756:   * 【829†before-dynamic-display-none.html†wpt.fyi】 【830†(live test)†wpt.live】 【831†(source)†github.com】\nL757:   * 【832†before-in-display-none-thcrash.html†wpt.fyi】 【833†(live test)†wpt.live】 【834†(source)†github.com】\nL758:   * 【835†before-preceding-whitespace-dynamic.html†wpt.fyi】 【836†(live test)†wpt.live】 【837†(source)†github.com】\nL759:   * 【838†focus-visible-originating-element.html†wpt.fyi】 【839†(live test)†wpt.live】 【840†(source)†github.com】\nL760: Both 【330†::before】 and 【331†::after】 are 【817†fully styleable pseudo-elements】: there is no restriction on what properties apply to them.\nL761: \nL762: For example, the following rule inserts the string “Note: ” before the content of every `<p>` element whose `class` attribute has the value `note`:\nL763: \nL764:     p.note::before { content: \"Note: \" }\nL765: Since the initial value of 【841†display】 is 【842†inline】, this will generate an inline box. Like other inline children of `<p>`, it will participate in `<p>`’s inline formatting context, potentially sharing a line with other content.\nL766: As with the content of regular elements, the generated content of 【330†::before】 and 【843†:after】 pseudo-elements can form part of any 【82†::first-line】 and 【25†::first-letter】 pseudo-elements applied to its 【83†originating element】. Also as with regular child elements, the ::before and 【331†::after】 pseudo-elements are suppressed when their parent, the originating element, is 【844†replaced】.\nL767: \nL768: Tests\nL769: \nL770:   * 【845†pseudo-replaced-elements.html†wpt.fyi】 【846†(live test)†wpt.live】 【847†(source)†github.com】\nL776:   * 【851†marker-and-other-pseudo-elements.html†wpt.fyi】 【852†(live test)†wpt.live】 【853†(source)†github.com】\nL777:   * 【854†marker-animate-002.html†wpt.fyi】 【855†(live test)†wpt.live】 【856†(source)†github.com】\nL778:   * 【857†marker-animate.html†wpt.fyi】 【858†(live test)†wpt.live】 【859†(source)†github.com】\nL779:   * 【860†marker-color.html†wpt.fyi】 【861†(live test)†wpt.live】 【862†(source)†github.com】\nL780:   * 【863†marker-computed-content.html†wpt.fyi】 【864†(live test)†wpt.live】 【865†(source)†github.com】\nL880: 【1089†::interest-button】 is a 【817†fully styleable pseudo-element】. When its computed 【821†content】 value is not 【822†none】, it generates boxes as if it were a following sibling of its 【83†originating element】, before any ::scroll-button() pseudo-elements that might also be on the originating element. It inherits from the originating element as normal.\nL892: ## 5. Element-backed Pseudo-Elements\nL893: \nL894: The element-backed pseudo-elements, interact with most CSS and other platform features as if they were real elements (and, in fact, often are real elements that are not otherwise selectable).\nL895: Element-backed pseudo-elements are always 【1062†tree-abiding】. Unless otherwise specified, they are 【817†fully styleable】 and inherit from their 【83†originating element】, just like standard tree-abiding pseudo-elements; but they can be defined to inherit from another element instead. (For example, 【1097†::part()】 inherits from the parent of the element it represents in the shadow tree.)\nL896: All 【571†pseudo-classes†www.w3.org】 and 【81†pseudo-elements】 are syntactically allowed after an 【1098†element-backed pseudo-element】 (such as x-button::part(label):hover or x-button::part(label)::before), just as if the pseudo-element were a 【651†type selector】; but some are disallowed from matching:\nL897: \nL898:   * The 【1099†structural pseudo-classes】, 【1100†:has()】 pseudo-class, 【1101†:scope】 pseudo-class, and 【1102†:host】/【1103†:host()】/【1104†:host-context()】 pseudo-classes never match.\nL899:   * 【1097†::part()】 never matches. (Other 【1098†element-backed pseudo-elements】 can, however.)\nL900: An 【1098†element-backed pseudo-element】 can define itself as representing a real element (possibly one not accessible in the current tree). If it does so, all pseudo-classes and pseudo-elements not otherwise disallowed (see above) match as they would on that real element. If it does not do so, it must define which pseudo-classes it matches and when; however, unless otherwise specified, any pseudo-classes allowed on 【1062†tree-abiding pseudo-elements】 are always allowed on element-backed pseudo-elements.\nL1042:   * Defined 【1098†element-backed pseudo-element】 and 【817†fully styleable pseudo-element】 as terms. (【1160†Issue 10199†github.com】, 【1161†Issue 10083†github.com】)\nL1043:   * Reworked the property (and custom property) application and inheritance model for 【491†highlight pseudo-elements】 (Issues 【1162†7591†github.com】, 【1163†7580†github.com】, 【1164†6641†github.com】, 【1165†11317†github.com】)\nL1044:   * Defined 【343†::highlight()】 and improved cross-referencing to 【652†[CSS-HIGHLIGHT-API-1]】. (Issue 【1166†6755†github.com】)\nL1048:   * Renamed ::postfix to 【24†::suffix】. (Issue 【1172†Issue 11949†github.com】)\nL1049:   * Excluded inline layout properties from 【1065†::placeholder】. (【1173†Issue 5379†github.com】)\nL1050:   * Clarified that UAs must not tweak author-specified colors for 【491†highlight pseudo-elements】. (【698†Issue 6853†github.com】)\nL1051:   * Clarified that the inherited value of 【183†color】 is 【744†currentColor】, not the 【745†initial value】.\nL1053:   * Added ::first-letter::prefix and ::first-letter::postfix 【317†sub-pseudo-elements】 to address punctuation associated with the 【25†::first-letter】 【81†pseudo-element】. (【1174†Issue 2040†github.com】)\nL1054:   * Fine-tuned the 【322†first-letter text】 pattern:\nL1055:     * Excluded word-separating spaces from 【322†first-letter text】. (【1175†Issue 5830†github.com】)\nL1056:     * Excluded dashes and opening punctuation from following punctuation. (【1175†Issue 5830†github.com】)\nL1160:   * 【82†::first-line】, in § 2.1\nL1161:   * 【817†fully styleable】, in § 4\nL1162:   * 【817†fully styleable pseudo-elements】, in § 4\nL1163:   * 【342†::grammar-error】, in § 3.1\nL1164:   * 【343†::highlight(<highlight-name-selector>)】, in § 3.1\nL1165:   * 【644†<highlight-name-selector>】, in § 3.1\nL1166:   * 【653†highlight overlay】, in § 3.4\nL1167:   * 【491†highlight pseudo-element】, in § 3.1\nL1168:   * 【1089†::interest-button】, in § 4.4\nL1169:   * 【848†::marker】, in § 4.2\nL1170:   * 【699†paired default highlight colors】, in § 3.3\nL1171:   * 【1136†parent】, in § 7.1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCSS Display Module Level 3 (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-3/)\nciteturn3600view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-3/\",\"pattern\":\"element itself does not generate\"}); Total lines: 1580\nL113: Similarly, each contiguous sequence of sibling 【80†text nodes】 generates a 【99†text sequence】 containing their text contents, which is assigned the same styles as the generating text nodes. If the sequence contains no text, however, it does not generate a text sequence.\nL554: contents\nL555:     The element itself does not generate any boxes, but its children and pseudo-elements still generate 【88†boxes】 and 【99†text sequences】 as normal. For the purposes of box generation and layout, the element must be treated as if it had been replaced in the 【102†element tree】 by its contents (including both its source-document children and its pseudo-elements, such as 【762†::before】 and 【763†::after】 pseudo-elements, which are generated before/after the element’s children as normal).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCSS Display Module Level 3 (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-3/)\nciteturn3600view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-3/\",\"pattern\":\"flex items\"}); Total lines: 1580\nL686: ## 3. Display Order: the 【1006†order】 property\nL687: \nL688: Name:  | order\nL689: 【144†Value:†www.w3.org】  | 【1007†<integer>】\nL690: 【153†Initial:†www.w3.org】  | 0\nL691: 【154†Applies to:†www.w3.org】  | 【1008†flex items】 and 【1009†grid items】\nL692: 【156†Inherited:†www.w3.org】  | no\nL693: 【157†Percentages:†www.w3.org】  | n/a\nL694: 【158†Computed value:†www.w3.org】  | specified integer\nL695: 【162†Canonical order:†www.w3.org】  | per grammar\nL696: 【163†Animation type:†www.w3.org】  | by computed value type\nL697: Tests\nL701: Specifically, the 【1006†order】 property controls the order in which 【1008†flex items】 or 【1009†grid items】 appear within their container, by assigning them to ordinal groups. It takes a single 【1007†<integer>】 value, which specifies which ordinal group the item belongs to.\nL702: Here’s an example of a catalog item card which has a title, a photo, and a description. Within each entry, the source document content is ordered logically with the title first, followed by the description and the photo. This provides a sensible ordering for speech rendering and in non-CSS browsers. For a more compelling visual presentation, however, 【1006†order】 is used to pull the image up from later in the content to the top of the card.\nL703: \nL704:     article.sale-item {\nL705:       display: flex;\nL738: 【182†Flex】 and 【185†grid containers】 lay out their contents in order-modified document order, starting from the lowest numbered ordinal group and going up. Items with the same ordinal group are laid out in the order they appear in the source document. This also affects the 【1014†painting order†www.w3.org】 【104†[CSS2]】, exactly as if the 【1008†flex】/【1009†grid items】 were reordered in the source document.\nL739: Absolutely-positioned children of a flex/grid container are treated as having 【1006†order: 0】 for the purpose of determining their painting order relative to flex/grid items.\nL740: Unless otherwise specified by a future specification, this property has no effect on boxes that are not 【1008†flex items】 or 【1009†grid items】.\nL741: ### 3.1. Reordering and Accessibility\nL742: \nL743: The 【1006†order】 property does not affect ordering in non-visual media (such as 【1015†speech†www.w3.org】). Likewise, order does not affect the default traversal order of sequential navigation modes (such as cycling through links, see e.g. 【1016†`tabindex`†html.spec.whatwg.org】 【1017†[HTML]】).\nL744: \nL745: Authors must use 【1006†order】 only for spatial, not logical, reordering of content. Style sheets that use order to perform logical reordering are non-conforming.\nL746: Note: This is so that non-visual media and non-CSS UAs, which typically present content linearly, can rely on a logical source order, while 【1006†order】 is used to tailor the layout order. (Since visual perception is two-dimensional and non-linear, the desired layout order is not always logical.)\nL747: In order to preserve the author’s intended ordering in all presentation modes, authoring tools—​including WYSIWYG editors as well as Web-based authoring aids—​must reorder the underlying document source and not use 【1006†order】 to perform reordering unless the author has explicitly indicated that the spatial order should be out-of-sync with the underlying document order (which determines speech and navigation order).\nL748: For example, a tool might offer both drag-and-drop reordering of flex items as well as handling of media queries for alternate layouts per screen size range.\nL749: Since most of the time, reordering should affect all screen ranges as well as navigation and speech order, the tool would perform drag-and-drop reordering at the DOM layer. In some cases, however, the author may want different layouts per screen size.\nL772:     Indicates that the box is collapsed, which can cause it to take up less space than otherwise in a formatting-context–specific way. See 【1020†dynamic row and column effects in tables†www.w3.org】 【104†[CSS2]】 and 【1021†collapsed flex items】 in flex layout 【731†[CSS-FLEXBOX-1]】. In all other cases, however, (i.e. unless otherwise specified) this simply makes the box 【1019†invisible】, just like 【1022†hidden】.\nL1577: 【1006†order】  | <integer>  | 0  | flex items and grid items  | no  | n/a  | by computed value type  | per grammar  | specified integer  |\nL1578: 【1018†visibility】  | visible | hidden | collapse  | visible  | all elements  | yes  | N/A  | discrete  | per grammar  | as specified  | visual\n"
